ance","source_section":"Statement","quote":"Let $(a_k)$ be a sequence of reals with partial sums $s_n = \\sum_{k<n} a_k$, let","uses":["2.2","4.2","6.1","8.1"]},{"fact":"L9","source":"def-real-limit","source_section":"Definition","quote":"A sequence $(x_k)$ of reals **converges** to $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ when for","uses":["2.2","4.2","6.1","8.1"]},{"fact":"L10","source":"thm-nonnegative-series-bounded-partial-sums","source_section":"Statement","quote":"This is the theorem that makes the nonnegative theory work: for terms of one","uses":["4.2"]},{"fact":"L11","source":"thm-squeeze","source_section":"Statement","quote":"theorem, and it is why the squeeze is a tool for *establishing* convergence","uses":["3.2","5.2","6.1"]},{"fact":"L11","source":"thm-algebra-of-limits","source_section":"Statement","quote":"Let $(x_k)$ and $(y_k)$ be sequences of reals ([[def-sequence]]) converging to","uses":["3.2","5.2","6.1"]},{"fact":"L11","source":"lem-limit-preserves-order","source_section":"Statement","quote":"The conclusion is **not** strict, and cannot be made strict; see the remarks","uses":["3.2","5.2","6.1"]}],"derivations":[{"id":"step-1-1","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 1.1.","step":"1.1","inputs":["L1","L2","L5","L7"]},{"id":"step-1-2","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 1.2.","step":"1.2","inputs":["L4","L1"]},{"id":"step-2-1","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 2.1.","step":"2.1","inputs":["1.1","L1","L3","L4"]},{"id":"step-2-2","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 2.2.","step":"2.2","inputs":["L9","1.2"]},{"id":"step-3-1","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 3.1.","step":"3.1","inputs":["1.1","2.1","L1","L3"]},{"id":"step-3-2","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 3.2.","step":"3.2","inputs":["2.2","1.2","L1","L2","L6","L11"]},{"id":"step-4-1","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 4.1.","step":"4.1","inputs":["3.1","L5"]},{"id":"step-4-2","claim":"Verified the stated inference at step 4.2.","st